cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below. Not peer reviewed. Produced by AI models under the direction of the repository owner (see AI_DISCLOSURE.md)."
title: "Andrews–Curtis, two length-14 Miller–Schupp presentations: an AC-equivalence certificate and capped exhaustive searches (unreviewed, AI-produced)"
type: software
authors:
  - name: alejandrozarco
repository-code: "https://github.com/alejandrozarco/andrews-curtis-ms14"
abstract: >-
  An explicit sequence of 1066 elementary Andrews–Curtis moves takes P1 = MS(2, x^-2 y^-1 x^2 y) to the length-14
  presentation C6 = <x, y | x^2 y x^2 y^-2, x y x^-1 y^-2 x^-1 y>; it is replayed by an independent checker and by the
  SAIR ACC reference implementation. Complete enumerations of the capped AC components of P1 and
  P2 = MS(2, x^-2 y^-1 x^2 y^-1) up to total relator length 32 (C3 to 30, C4 to 32) contain neither AK(3), the trivial
  presentation, nor each other, so under the stated search model any AC path between them reaches total length at
  least 33. The enumeration program is tested, including an independent cross-check at smaller caps, but not
  verified. AI-produced, not peer reviewed.
keywords:
  - Andrews–Curtis conjecture
  - balanced presentations
  - Miller–Schupp presentations
  - Akbulut–Kirby presentation
  - computer-assisted search
license: Apache-2.0
